{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUR8pQVCuJnt6yYQ9WHPrt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-227 — Run-menu trailing arguments: decide the contract, then quote it (repo-review-2026-07-18 M-06)\n2\t\n3\t**Branch:** dualplan-routing-fix · **Filed:** 2026-07-18 (review M-06) ·\n4\t**BuildTier:** medium · **SafetyClass:** ordinary (launcher convenience\n5\tlayer; not the dispatcher).\n6\t\n7\t## Why\n8\t\n9\t`run_menu.py:116` concatenates trailing user arguments into a shell command\n10\tstring unquoted. An argument containing spaces or shell metacharacters\n11\tsplits or executes differently than the user intended, and Windows\n12\t(`cmd.exe`) vs POSIX quoting rules differ, so a naive quoting patch is\n13\tunsafe without deciding what the contract *is*. The review deliberately left\n14\tthis unfixed pending that decision (§0 table).\n15\t\n16\t## Scope\n17\t\n18\t1. **Decide the contract** (recorded in this spec as a ruling section,\n19\t   WI-223-style): either trailing arguments are a **trusted shell fragment**\n20\t   (documented as such — the user owns quoting; the kit passes it through\n21\t   verbatim on both platforms) or they are **data arguments** (the kit\n22\t   appends them as argv items with per-platform quoting, never re-parsed by\n23\t   a shell). The recommendation is data-arguments: menu entries are the\n24\t   trusted recipes; user-supplied trailing args are values.\n25\t2. **Implement** the ruled semantics explicitly — argv-append or documented\n26\t   passthrough — with tests covering spaces, quotes, and `&`/`|`\n27\t   metacharacters on both Windows and POSIX (skip-guarded like the suite's\n28\t   existing shell-dependent tests).\n29\t\n30\t**Non-goals:** no menu-format redesign; no change to how the menu's own\n31\trecipe lines execute.\n32\t\n33\t## Done-when\n34\t\n35\tThe ruling recorded; behavior implemented per ruling with cross-platform\n36\tregression tests proven failing pre-fix under the ruled semantics; smoke bar\n37\tgreen per commit, full suite at close.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e26fa48-d747-4d44-a15a-1e1f5c67afa8","uuid":"26dfd6ca-4c36-4a7d-ab6d-0b19533dc18d","timestamp":"2026-07-18T22:05:33.845Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-227-cec3\\docs\\specs\\WI-227.md","content":"# WI-227 — Run-menu trailing arguments: decide the contract, then quote it (repo-review-2026-07-18 M-06)\n\n**Branch:** dualplan-routing-fix · **Filed:** 2026-07-18 (review M-06) ·\n**BuildTier:** medium · **SafetyClass:** ordinary (launcher convenience\nlayer; not the dispatcher).\n\n## Why\n\n`run_menu.py:116` concatenates trailing user arguments into a shell command\nstring unquoted. An argument containing spaces or shell metacharacters\nsplits or executes differently than the user intended, and Windows\n(`cmd.exe`) vs POSIX quoting rules differ, so a naive quoting patch is\nunsafe without deciding what the contract *is*. The review deliberately left\nthis unfixed pending that decision (§0 table).\n\n## Scope\n\n1. **Decide the contract** (recorded in this spec as a ruling section,\n   WI-223-style): either trailing arguments are a **trusted shell fragment**\n   (documented as such — the user owns quoting; the kit passes it through\n   verbatim on both platforms) or they are **data arguments** (the kit\n   appends them as argv items with per-platform quoting, never re-parsed by\n   a shell). The recommendation is data-arguments: menu entries are the\n   trusted recipes; user-supplied trailing args are values.\n2. **Implement** the ruled semantics explicitly — argv-append or documented\n   passthrough — with tests covering spaces, quotes, and `&`/`|`\n   metacharacters on both Windows and POSIX (skip-guarded like the suite's\n   existing shell-dependent tests).\n\n**Non-goals:** no menu-format redesign; no change to how the menu's own\nrecipe lines execute.\n\n## Done-when\n\nThe ruling recorded; behavior implemented per ruling with cross-platform\nregression tests proven failing pre-fix under the ruled semantics; smoke bar\ngreen per commit, full suite at close.\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
