{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WEAGfkS7zJN4ASjVXqsCSt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"The run capability menu — one launcher that presents every major capability.\n3\t\n4\tThe root `run.cmd` / `run.sh` / `run.command` launchers are thin delegates to\n5\tthis script (process.md §7, \"the evaluator's rungs\"): running the product must\n6\tnever depend on recalling a command. Capabilities are **declared once** in\n7\t`docs/stack.ini`'s `[run]` section and read here, so the launch command lives in\n8\texactly one place instead of being duplicated across the platform launchers.\n9\t\n10\t`docs/stack.ini` `[run]` section format:\n11\t\n12\t    [run]\n13\t    serve = docker compose up -d && python -m webbrowser http://localhost:8080\n14\t    serve.desc = start the app and open its page\n15\t    iso = ./build_iso.sh\n16\t    iso.desc = build the bootable ISO and launch the burner\n17\t\n18\tOne `<name> = <command>` line per capability (in declaration order), plus an\n19\toptional `<name>.desc = <one line>`. Each command is a full **shell line** — a\n20\tmulti-step capability keeps its steps in a project script and names it here once.\n21\t\n22\tUsage (what the launchers invoke as `run_menu.py \"$@\"`):\n23\t    run_menu.py            no args  -> a numbered interactive menu (pick one)\n24\t    run_menu.py <name>     direct launch of that capability (exit code passes through)\n25\t    run_menu.py --list     stable machine-readable listing (the agent surface)\n26\t\n27\t`--list` prints one capability per line as `name<TAB>desc` (desc empty when none),\n28\tin declaration order — a parse-stable contract for agents/scripts; it exits 0 with\n29\tempty output when nothing is declared. The interactive and direct paths instead\n30\tprint the same \"no run capability wired yet\" guidance and exit 1 on an absent or\n31\tempty `[run]` section, exactly as the pre-menu launchers did — a pure library\n32\tsimply deletes the `run.*` launchers.\n33\t\n34\tStdlib-only, Python 3.8+, Windows + POSIX (the same portability contract as the\n35\trest of the kit). The command is run with `shell=True`: the value is the user's\n36\town declared shell line from their own `docs/stack.ini` (the same trust boundary\n37\tas the `RUN_CMD` this replaced — the user edits their own file), and a capability\n38\tis deliberately a full shell command (pipes, `&&`, redirects), so it is handed to\n39\tthe shell verbatim rather than split into argv.\n40\t\n41\tContracts: IF-048, IF-049 — the interface seams this module declares (process.md §8; rows of record in docs/requirements/interfaces.csv).\n42\t\"\"\"\n43\t\n44\timport argparse\n45\timport configparser\n46\timport subprocess\n47\timport sys\n48\tfrom pathlib import Path\n49\t\n50\t# The declared toolchain, read at repo root when present (the launchers cd there\n51\t# first). Same file check.py reads; this script only ever touches its [run]\n52\t# section, which check.py ignores.\n53\tDEFAULT_STACK_INI = Path(\"docs/stack.ini\")\n54\t\n55\t\n56\tdef _utf8_console():\n57\t    \"\"\"Emit UTF-8 to stdout/stderr whatever the OS console codepage is, so a\n58\t    non-ASCII capability name / desc / command banner can't raise\n59\t    UnicodeEncodeError on a legacy Windows cp1252 console (the sibling scripts'\n60\t    guard). Python 3.7+ streams expose `.reconfigure`; guard for the rest.\"\"\"\n61\t    for s in (sys.stdout, sys.stderr):\n62\t        try:\n63\t            s.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n64\t        except (AttributeError, ValueError):\n65\t            pass\n66\t\n67\t\n68\tdef load_capabilities(path):\n69\t    \"\"\"Parse the `[run]` section of a stack.ini into an ordered list of\n70\t    (name, command, desc). Returns [] when the file or section is absent/empty.\n71\t\n72\t    Declaration order is preserved (configparser is insertion-ordered), key case\n73\t    is preserved (a capability may be `Serve`), and `interpolation=None` keeps a\n74\t    literal `%`/`{}` in a command untouched. A malformed profile fails LOUDLY —\n75\t    a typo can't quietly hide a capability. A `<name>.desc` with no matching\n76\t    `<name> =` command, or a command with an empty value, is ignored.\"\"\"\n77\t    if not path.exists():\n78\t        return []\n79\t    cp = configparser.ConfigParser(interpolation=None)\n80\t    cp.optionxform = str  # preserve capability-name case\n81\t    try:\n82\t        cp.read_string(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"), source=str(path))\n83\t    except configparser.Error as exc:\n84\t        sys.exit(\"run_menu: {} is malformed: {}\".format(path, exc))\n85\t    if not cp.has_section(\"run\"):\n86\t        return []\n87\t    descs = {}\n88\t    commands = []\n89\t    for key, val in cp.items(\"run\"):\n90\t        if key.endswith(\".desc\"):\n91\t            descs[key[: -len(\".desc\")]] = val.strip()\n92\t        else:\n93\t            commands.append((key, val.strip()))\n94\t    return [(name, cmd, descs.get(name, \"\")) for name, cmd in commands if cmd]\n95\t\n96\t\n97\tNO_CAPABILITIES = (\n98\t    \"run_menu: no run capabilities declared yet.\\n\"\n99\t    \"Declare them in docs/stack.ini under a [run] section, one line each:\\n\"\n100\t    \"  [run]\\n\"\n101\t    \"  serve = python -m yourapp\\n\"\n102\t    \"  serve.desc = start the app\\n\"\n103\t    \"The README 'Run it' section documents the underlying commands.\\n\"\n104\t    \"(A pure library has none — delete the run.* launchers.)\"\n105\t)\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tdef launch(command, extra):\n109\t    \"\"\"Run a capability's shell line, returning its exit code (passthrough).\n110\t\n111\t    `extra` (trailing args the launcher forwarded) is appended to the command\n112\t    line, mirroring the old `exec $RUN_CMD \"$@\"` passthrough. shell=True is\n113\t    intentional — see the module docstring.\"\"\"\n114\t    full = command if not extra else command + \" \" + \" \".join(extra)\n115\t    print(\"Running: {}\".format(full), flush=True)\n116\t    return subprocess.run(full, shell=True).returncode\n117\t\n118\t\n119\tdef direct(capabilities, name, extra):\n120\t    \"\"\"Launch the named capability, or report the valid names and exit 2.\"\"\"\n121\t    for cap_name, command, _desc in capabilities:\n122\t        if cap_name == name:\n123\t            return launch(command, extra)\n124\t    print(\n125\t        \"run_menu: no capability named {!r}. Declared: {}\".format(\n126\t            name, \", \".join(n for n, _, _ in capabilities) or \"(none)\"\n127\t        ),\n128\t        file=sys.stderr,\n129\t    )\n130\t    return 2\n131\t\n132\t\n133\tdef interactive_menu(capabilities):\n134\t    \"\"\"Present the numbered menu, read a pick from stdin, launch it.\n135\t\n136\t    Reads from stdin (a TTY when double-clicked, a piped selection otherwise);\n137\t    an EOF (closed/exhausted stdin) ends the loop rather than hanging, so an\n138\t    unattended invocation is safe. `q`/`quit`/blank quits with exit 0.\"\"\"\n139\t    print(\"Run — available capabilities:\\n\")\n140\t    for i, (name, _command, desc) in enumerate(capabilities, 1):\n141\t        line = \"  {}) {}\".format(i, name)\n142\t        if desc:\n143\t            line += \" — \" + desc\n144\t        print(line)\n145\t    print()\n146\t    while True:\n147\t        try:\n148\t            raw = input(\"Select [1-{}] (q to quit): \".format(len(capabilities)))\n149\t        except EOFError:\n150\t            print(\"run_menu: no selection (input closed).\", file=sys.stderr)\n151\t            return 1\n152\t        raw = raw.strip()\n153\t        if raw.lower() in (\"\", \"q\", \"quit\"):\n154\t            return 0\n155\t        try:\n156\t            choice = int(raw)\n157\t        except ValueError:\n158\t            choice = 0\n159\t        if 1 <= choice <= len(capabilities):\n160\t            _name, command, _desc = capabilities[choice - 1]\n161\t            return launch(command, [])\n162\t        print(\"  not a valid choice; enter 1-{} or q.\".format(len(capabilities)))\n163\t\n164\t\n165\tdef main(argv=None):\n166\t    _utf8_console()\n167\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n168\t        description=\"Present/launch the capabilities declared in docs/stack.ini [run].\",\n169\t        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,\n170\t    )\n171\t    ap.add_argument(\n172\t        \"--list\",\n173\t        action=\"store_true\",\n174\t        help=\"print a stable machine listing (name<TAB>desc, one per line) and exit 0\",\n175\t    )\n176\t    ap.add_argument(\n177\t        \"--file\",\n178\t        default=str(DEFAULT_STACK_INI),\n179\t        help=\"stack.ini to read the [run] section from (default: docs/stack.ini)\",\n180\t    )\n181\t    ap.add_argument(\n182\t        \"name\",\n183\t        nargs=\"?\",\n184\t        help=\"a capability name to launch directly (no name = the interactive menu)\",\n185\t    )\n186\t    ap.add_argument(\n187\t        \"args\",\n188\t        nargs=argparse.REMAINDER,\n189\t        help=\"trailing args forwarded to the launched command\",\n190\t    )\n191\t    ns = ap.parse_args(argv)\n192\t\n193\t    capabilities = load_capabilities(Path(ns.file))\n194\t\n195\t    if ns.list:\n196\t        # The agent surface: parse-stable, empty when nothing is declared (an\n197\t        # agent reads zero lines rather than guidance prose on stdout).\n198\t        for name, _command, desc in capabilities:\n199\t            print(\"{}\\t{}\".format(name, desc))\n200\t        return 0\n201\t\n202\t    if not capabilities:\n203\t        print(NO_CAPABILITIES, file=sys.stderr)\n204\t        return 1\n205\t\n206\t    if ns.name is not None:\n207\t        return direct(capabilities, ns.name, ns.args)\n208\t    return interactive_menu(capabilities)\n209\t\n210\t\n211\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n212\t    sys.exit(main())\n213\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e26fa48-d747-4d44-a15a-1e1f5c67afa8","uuid":"7351459f-bd2f-494c-ac36-eaff28d9b82d","timestamp":"2026-07-18T22:05:37.341Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-227-cec3\\project-trajectory\\scripts\\run_menu.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"The run capability menu — one launcher that presents every major capability.\n\nThe root `run.cmd` / `run.sh` / `run.command` launchers are thin delegates to\nthis script (process.md §7, \"the evaluator's rungs\"): running the product must\nnever depend on recalling a command. Capabilities are **declared once** in\n`docs/stack.ini`'s `[run]` section and read here, so the launch command lives in\nexactly one place instead of being duplicated across the platform launchers.\n\n`docs/stack.ini` `[run]` section format:\n\n    [run]\n    serve = docker compose up -d && python -m webbrowser http://localhost:8080\n    serve.desc = start the app and open its page\n    iso = ./build_iso.sh\n    iso.desc = build the bootable ISO and launch the burner\n\nOne `<name> = <command>` line per capability (in declaration order), plus an\noptional `<name>.desc = <one line>`. Each command is a full **shell line** — a\nmulti-step capability keeps its steps in a project script and names it here once.\n\nUsage (what the launchers invoke as `run_menu.py \"$@\"`):\n    run_menu.py            no args  -> a numbered interactive menu (pick one)\n    run_menu.py <name>     direct launch of that capability (exit code passes through)\n    run_menu.py --list     stable machine-readable listing (the agent surface)\n\n`--list` prints one capability per line as `name<TAB>desc` (desc empty when none),\nin declaration order — a parse-stable contract for agents/scripts; it exits 0 with\nempty output when nothing is declared. The interactive and direct paths instead\nprint the same \"no run capability wired yet\" guidance and exit 1 on an absent or\nempty `[run]` section, exactly as the pre-menu launchers did — a pure library\nsimply deletes the `run.*` launchers.\n\nStdlib-only, Python 3