{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdAJJ6yb6yjtQJQQhgTjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SxmiaG5ovS5GBpJvjkRzZ4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Projects/ai-template-trains/1-g3-WI-227-cec3\" && git add docs/specs/WI-227.md project-trajectory/scripts/run_menu.py tests/test_run_menu.py && git commit -F - <<'EOF'\nWI-227: rule run-menu trailing args as data, quote them cross-platform\n\nThe run-menu forwarded trailing launcher args into the shell recipe\nunquoted (`command + \" \" + \" \".join(extra)`), so a value with spaces\nsplit into two tokens and an `&`/`|` executed as a shell operator —\ndifferently on cmd.exe vs POSIX. The review (M-06) left it unfixed\npending a contract decision.\n\nRuling (recorded in the spec, WI-223-style): trailing args are DATA\nvalues, not shell text. The declared `[run]` recipe stays the trusted\nshell line; each forwarded arg is now appended quoted for the platform\nshell so it reaches the program as exactly one literal token —\n`shlex.quote` on POSIX (total), a double-quoted cmd.exe/MSVCRT token on\nWindows (separators/redirects inside are literal). Two Windows-only\nlimits (`%VAR%` expansion; a quote-plus-separator value) are cmd.exe\nparser facts, documented in the module docstring rather than fought.\n\nTests: a parametrized case per space/`&`/`|`/`&&`/embedded-quote proven\nfailing pre-fix on this box, plus a POSIX-guarded shell-expansion\nneutralization test. run_menu suite 16p/1s; full suite 1049p/35s;\nruff + duplicate-code gate clean.\n\nWI: WI-227\nTrain: 1-g3-WI-227-cec3\nBase: 808f95da957c1ce90476e8807acb784159255107\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":87089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_token