{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdAJL2sLndKPjLpt2ytFD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-227 is complete and committed (`abff35b`) on `llm/train/1-g3-WI-227-cec3`.\n\n## What I did\n\n**Decided the contract (the ruling).** Recorded a WI-223-style *Ruling — data arguments* section in `docs/specs/WI-227.md`: trailing launcher args are **data values, not shell text**. The declared `[run]` recipe stays a trusted `shell=True` line; each forwarded arg is appended *quoted for the platform shell* so it lands as exactly one literal token — never re-split on whitespace, never re-parsed as an operator. I chose data-arguments (the spec's recommendation) because the recipe is trusted but an evaluator's `\"$@\"` is a value; passthrough-verbatim would make every trailing arg a per-platform quoting trap.\n\n**Implemented it** in `project-trajectory/scripts/run_menu.py`:\n- `_quote_extra` dispatches per platform — `shlex.quote` on POSIX (total), `_win_quote` on Windows.\n- `_win_quote` force-wraps each token in double quotes (so cmd.exe treats `& | < > ( ) ^` as literal) with the MSVCRT backslash/quote escaping the target program's argv parser needs.\n- Documented the two genuine cmd.exe-parser limits (`%VAR%` expansion; a quote-*plus*-separator value) in the module docstring rather than pretending to fix them — this is an ordinary convenience layer.\n\n**Validated empirically first.** Before writing the fix I drove real cmd.exe with candidate quoting and confirmed exactly which cases work (spaces, `&`, `|`, `&&`, `^`, `()`, `!`, backslashes, lone `\"`) and which are the residual Windows limits — so the ruling's claims are grounded, not guessed.\n\n**Tests, proven failing pre-fix.** Added a parametrized test (space, `&`, `|`, `&&`, embedded quote) asserting each arrives as one literal token, plus a POSIX-guarded shell-expansion-neutralization test. I reverted the one-line fix and confirmed all 5 parametrized cases **fail** pre-fix, then restored it and confirmed green.\n\n## Verification\n- ruff format `--check` + lint: clean\n- run_menu suite: 16 passed, 1 skipped\n- smoke tier: **850 passed, 3 skipped**\n- full unfiltered suite: **1049 passed, 35 skipped**\n- duplicate-code gate: OK; all pre-commit hooks PASS\n\nI did not touch any root coordination truth (status.md, run-state, log.md, work-items.csv Status/Deliverable cells, or generated artifacts) — the integrator regenerates those at integration."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_read_input_tokens":90442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e26fa48-d747-4d44-a15a-1e1f5c67afa8","uuid":"3728cc86-6ad2-4d96-8cac-b98439a59bb1","request_id":"req_011CdAJKzzj3qicdfGgv1opA"}
